A DP model for K1.6Mg0.8Ti7.2O16 crystalline with space group of I4/m. DP-GEN, a concurrent learning platform specifically designed for generating high-reliability datasets, comprises a sequence of iterative cycles. The initial training dataset was generated using the init\_bulk module. Specifically, the unit cell was subjected to scaling and minor perturbations of atomic positions, followed by the performance of 20 steps of ab initio molecular dynamics (AIMD) simulations. Then, the following each iteration consists of three consecutive steps: training, exploration, and labeling. During the training phase, four deep potential models with distinct random seeds were developed using the DeepMD-kit package. The training process for these deep potentials spanned 2×105 steps. The embedding network was constructed with three fully connected layers containing 25, 50, and 100 nodes respectively, while the fitting network featured three layers, each equipped with 100 nodes. A long training of all labeled structures is employed for 5×106 steps to get the final deep potential.